Read headless frames back without stalling the GPU

Each headless frame was drawn to a new image, which BlitScreen took for a
size change: it waited for the device to go idle and rebuilt its pass
every frame, and the readback then waited for the GPU again. The GPU
thread stalled twice a frame.

Keep a few frames with their download buffers, and copy each one back on
a readback thread once the GPU has finished it. The thread publishes the
frame under a lock that retro_run holds while it uploads, so a frame no
longer changes while the frontend reads it.

